WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.570
Two phone plans.

2
00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:05.830
Plan A costs twelve pounds a
month, plus eight pence a minute.

3
00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:10.230
Plan B costs twenty pounds a
month, plus three pence a minute.

4
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.640
Start the clock.

5
00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:14.880
As the minutes tick by,
both bills creep up,

6
00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:16.360
at different speeds.

7
00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.580
Plan B starts dearer.

8
00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:20.500
Will A ever catch up?

9
00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.510
When does the pricier plan
become the cheaper one?

10
00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.050
In this mission, you'll write
each cost as an expression:

11
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.430
a fixed charge plus a
rate times the units.

12
00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.710
You'll set two expressions equal, and
solve an equation with the unknown on both

13
00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:35.680
sides.

14
00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:40.850
And you'll use an inequality to say
when one quantity is less than another.

15
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:45.170
Your mission: find when the pricier
phone plan becomes the cheaper one.
